<div class="wrap-narrow">
  <header class="page-head">
    <span class="eyebrow">Limits</span>
    <h1>What eui-score does not engrave</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Anything outside the subset is refused, with the character where the engraver stopped. The messages below
      are not copied in: each source is handed to the engraver when this page is shown, and its answer is what
      gets printed.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <% for refusal in refusals %>
      <div class="refusal">
        <h3><%= refusal["what"] %></h3>
        <pre><code><%- score_highlight(refusal["src"]) %></code></pre>
        <% if refusal["message"].nil? %>
          <p class="muted">Accepted by this version of the engraver.</p>
        <% else %>
          <p class="score-error"><%= refusal["message"] %></p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <h2>No longer limits</h2>
    <p>
      Since EUI 0.11 (Soli 2.28.2), the engraver reads LilyPond as people write it: variables and
      <code>\global</code>, <code>\new Voice</code> with <code>\voiceOne</code>/<code>\voiceTwo</code>,
      <code>\new Lyrics \lyricsto</code>, <code>\language</code>, <code>\fixed</code>, <code>\transpose</code>,
      <code>q</code>, <code>\partial</code>, <code>\cadenzaOn</code>, spacers, <code>\repeat unfold</code> and
      <code>percent</code>, grace notes, the tenor, soprano, baritone and <code>treble_8</code> clefs, fingerings,
      <code>\markup</code>, <code>\mark</code>, <code>\ottava</code>, phrasing slurs, <code>\trill</code> and other
      ornaments, <code>\arpeggio</code>, <code>\glissando</code>, tremolos, and <code>\new ChordNames</code>,
      <code>\new DrumStaff</code> and <code>\new TabStaff</code> — each drawn as LilyPond 2.25 draws it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since Soli 2.28.4, the server engraves with the same engraver as the browser: 64th and 128th notes, a
      tuplet inside a tuplet, up to four voices on a staff, several <code>\addlyrics</code> verses, any metre;
      a note longer than what is left of its bar is cut at the bar line into tied notes, as LilyPond's
      <code>Completion_heads_engraver</code> cuts it; the sustain pedal (<code>\sustainOn</code>,
      <code>\sustainOff</code>) is drawn and held; and LilyPond 2.24's jumps, <code>\jump "D.S. al Coda"</code>
      and <code>\fine</code>, are set against their bar line. The library, the shared pages and the PDFs show
      what the editor shows.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Layout</strong>: no cross-staff notation, and a page breaker simpler than LilyPond's.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="callout">
      Not sure? Paste your source into the <a href="<%= playground_path() %>">playground</a>: the engraver's
      message points at the exact character where it stops.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
